# monotorgba

- Label: Mono to RGBA
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 2
- Parameters: 2 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/monotorgba.html
- Summary (EN): Converts a mono layer into an RGBA layer, making the channel extension explicit (GGGG or GGG1) and optionally supplying a specific alpha layer. The node does not apply premultiplication.
- Résumé (FR) : Convertit un calque mono en RGBA en dupliquant son canal, avec un alpha optionnel fourni par un second calque, sans prémultiplication.

- Inputs meaning: ["mono: the original mono layer to convert", "alpha (optional): a mono layer used as the alpha channel of the result"]

- Key parameters: ["Fill Alpha: how alpha is created when no alpha layer is given. Use Mono as Alpha uses the input mono layer as alpha; Constant Value sets a fixed alpha", "Alpha Value: the alpha applied when Fill Alpha is Constant Value"]

- Caveats: ["No premultiplication is applied.", "By default the mono layer is replicated to RGB and alpha, which gives a white image with varying alpha for premultiplied layers. This can be unexpected.", "The alpha input is mixed without premultiplication, so the Premultiply COP may be needed."]

